What changed: the report is now one rule for both teardown paths, called before
proc_clear_resume_state() drops the poison identity — process_kill (normal
kill/exit) and process_exit (the #PF path, and SYS_SLS_EXIT). B7's carve-out for
fault exits is gone: an adopted tenant that produces no exit line now reddens
the clause.

