=== the clause's failure side after the tightening ===
Before this run, the tightened clause was replayed against two recordings whose
tenant was adopted and which had no exit line: the FIRST run's no-heap
recording and the control with its exit line removed. Both reddened with the
same sentence — "the resumed tenant's teardown has no exit scan — the report
rides process_kill and process_exit, so an adopted tenant produces one on
either path, fault included" — so the carve-out is now covered by a named red,
not by a pass.

After the run, the control recording with its exit line duplicated reddened the
same clause with "the teardown reported the stack 2 times" — the two paths are
kept exclusive by B7's count, not only by the kernel's structure.

